<div class="grid-3">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Composite z-score</span>
      <span class="v {% if sentiment.composite_score >= 0 %}pos{% else %}neg{% endif %}">{{ '{:+.3f}'.format(sentiment.composite_score) }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Active signals</span>
      <span class="v">{{ sentiment.composite_n_signals }} of 3</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Sources</span>
      <span class="v">{{ sentiment.sources_available | join(', ') if sentiment.sources_available else '-' }}</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">StockTwits bull</span>
      <span class="v pos">{{ sentiment.stocktwits_bull_count }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">StockTwits bear</span>
      <span class="v neg">{{ sentiment.stocktwits_bear_count }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">StockTwits net</span>
      <span class="v {% if sentiment.stocktwits_net_sentiment >= 0 %}pos{% else %}neg{% endif %}">{{ '{:+.2f}'.format(sentiment.stocktwits_net_sentiment) }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Message volume</span>
      <span class="v">{{ sentiment.stocktwits_message_volume }}</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">ApeWisdom mentions</span>
      <span class="v">{{ sentiment.apewisdom_mentions }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">24h change</span>
      <span class="v {% if sentiment.apewisdom_mentions_24h_change >= 0 %}pos{% else %}neg{% endif %}">{{ '{:+d}'.format(sentiment.apewisdom_mentions_24h_change) }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Reddit rank</span>
      <span class="v">{{ sentiment.apewisdom_rank if sentiment.apewisdom_rank else '-' }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">25-delta IV skew</span>
      <span class="v">{{ '{:+.4f}'.format(sentiment.iv_skew_25d) if sentiment.iv_skew_25d is not none else '-' }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">IV-skew read</span>
      <span class="v"><span class="tag {% if sentiment.iv_skew_interpretation == 'bullish' %}tag-green{% elif sentiment.iv_skew_interpretation == 'bearish' %}tag-red{% else %}tag-blue{% endif %}">{{ sentiment.iv_skew_interpretation }}</span></span></div>
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

{% if critique %}
<h2>Analyst critique</h2>
<div class="grid-2">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Agreement with model</span>
      <span class="v"><span class="tag {% if critique.agreement == 'agree' %}tag-green{% elif critique.agreement == 'disagree' %}tag-red{% else %}tag-orange{% endif %}">{{ critique.agreement }}</span></span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Confidence</span>
      <span class="v">{{ critique.confidence }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">PM one-liner</span>
      <span class="v">{{ critique.one_line_pm_summary }}</span></div>
    <div class="kv"><span class="k">Sensitivity concern</span>
      <span class="v">{{ critique.sensitivity_concern }}</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <h3 style="color: var(--orange); margin: 0 0 6px 0;">What the model may have missed</h3>
    <ul class="risk-list">
      {% for m in critique.what_the_model_missed %}<li>{{ m }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% if critique.flags %}
    <h3 style="color: var(--accent2); margin: 12px 0 6px 0;">Critique flags</h3>
    <ul class="risk-list" style="color: var(--accent2);">
      {% for f in critique.flags %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2 style="color: var(--accent2);">Factor contribution methodology &mdash; where the numbers come from</h2>
<div class="card full">
  <div style="color: var(--fg2); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.55;">
    <p><b>Point return formula (linear factor model)</b>:
    <code style="background:var(--bg3);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:3px;">r_hat = alpha + sum_i (w_i &times; f_i)</code>
    where <code>w_i</code> is the cross-sectional loading for factor <i>i</i>
    (estimated from the cross-section of US large-cap names) and <code>f_i</code> is the
    z-scored factor value for this ticker (Grinold-Kahn winsorization at &plusmn;3).
    </p>
    <p><b>Per-factor contribution</b> shown in the waterfall above is exactly
    <code>w_i &times; f_i</code> (decimal-return units), so the bars sum (with intercept) to
    the linear forecast point. The <i>ensemble</i> point combines linear / Monte Carlo /
    AR(1) / random-walk per per-method-comparison table.</p>
    <p><b>Bias mapping (composite z-score &rarr; LONG/NEUTRAL/SHORT)</b>:
    weighted sum of value (1.0), quality (0.7), momentum (1.0), low-vol (0.5), revisions (1.0),
    news-activity (0.6); thresholds &plusmn;1.0 with macro override (risk-off +
    LONG &rarr; reduce to NEUTRAL; risk-on-growth + SHORT &rarr; reduce to NEUTRAL).
    LONG &rarr; long-bias screen (long-call / call-debit-spread / covered-call); SHORT &rarr;
    short-bias screen (long-put / put-debit-spread / bear-call-spread); NEUTRAL &rarr; cash.</p>
    <p><b>Sensitivity</b> (one-factor-at-a-time tornado above): impact = <code>w_i &times; 1sd</code>
    per factor (MSCI / Two-Sigma Venn convention). Stress scenarios are canned multi-factor
    shocks (rates +100bps; recession risk-off; quality flight).</p>
    <p><b>Factor decay</b> uses exponential half-life per factor type:
    catalysts 7d, news 14d, revisions 30d, momentum 45d, value 90d, quality 90d
    (Tetlock 2007; Cohen-Malloy-Pomorski 2012). The heatmap above shows
    <code>contribution &times; exp(-ln(2) &times; t / half_life)</code> on a 5-day grid.</p>
    <p><b>Factor IC backtest</b>: Spearman rank correlation between each factor's
    cross-sectional ranking on day <i>t</i> and the realized <i>h</i>-day-forward
    return, aggregated across the panel (Grinold-Kahn 2000 ch.4 fundamental law of
    active management). Source for this report: <code>{{ ic_backtest_provenance }}</code>.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>Catalysts in window ({{ horizon_days }}d)</h2>
<div class="card full">
{% if catalysts %}
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Date</th><th>Type</th><th>Source</th><th>Confidence</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    {% for cat in catalysts %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ cat.catalyst_date }}</td>
        <td><span class="tag tag-orange">{{ cat.catalyst_type }}</span></td>
        <td>{{ cat.source }}</td>
        <td>{{ cat.confidence }}</td>
        <td>{{ cat.catalyst_description or '' }}</td>
      </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
{% else %}
  <em style="color: var(--muted);">No catalysts within the forecast window.</em>
{% endif %}
</div>

<h2>Analyst narrative</h2>
<div class="grid-2">
  <div class="narrative-card bull">
    <h3>Bull case</h3>
    <div>{{ narrative.bull_case }}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="narrative-card bear">
    <h3>Bear case</h3>
    <div>{{ narrative.bear_case }}</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="narrative-card syn" style="margin-top: 12px;">
  <h3>Synthesis</h3>
  <div>{{ narrative.synthesis }}</div>
</div>
{% if narrative.risk_flags %}
<div class="card full" style="margin-top: 12px;">
  <h3 style="color: var(--orange); margin-top: 0;">Risk flags</h3>
  <ul class="risk-list">
  {% for f in narrative.risk_flags %}<li>{{ f }}</li>{% endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
{% endif %}

<div class="footer">
  Generated by Trade Identifier Forecast Layer v{{ report_v2_version }} (dark mode).
  Ensemble methodology: linear multi-factor regression + GBM Monte Carlo + AR(1) + random-walk baseline.
  Factor decay: exponential half-life per factor type (Tetlock 2007; Cohen-Malloy-Pomorski 2012).
  Macro context: 10y / 3m Treasury yields + VIX z-score + sector ETF relative strength.
  Narrative source: {{ narrative.source }}{% if narrative.source == 'claude' %} (Anthropic Claude){% else %} (deterministic template fallback){% endif %}.
  Not investment advice.
</div>

</body>
</html>
